    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0508" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Strobel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1888</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 324.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Curry’s No. 280, of the
                    22d November last, relating to the imprisonment of the Rev. E. T. Doane at
                    Ponape, in the Caroline Islands, I inclose a copy of a letter recently received
                    from the Rev. Judson Smith and of the Department’s reply thereto.</p>
                <p>You will call the attention of the Spanish Government to the matter in the sense
                    of the Department’s letter to Mr. Smith.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>




